# Canonicalize an accidental trailing slash on a real route to the
# no-trailing-slash form used everywhere internally (nav, footer, sitemap)
# via a real 301, rather than letting it fall through to the 404 catch-all
# below or serve as an accidental second URL for the same content. Must
# come before the exact-match rewrites so it takes priority for these
# specific paths.
/products/           /products             301
/export-solutions/   /export-solutions     301
/wholesale/          /wholesale            301
/export/             /export               301
/about/              /about                301
/contact/            /contact              301

# Explicit rewrite for every real public route (matches sitemap.xml and
# client/src/App.tsx's route table) so the SPA shell loads with a 200.
# Anything else falls through to the wildcard below with a real 404 status
# instead of a soft 404 — previously *every* unknown path (typos, removed
# URLs, bots probing random paths) returned 200 with the homepage's raw
# HTML, which is exactly what search engines flag as a soft-404 signal.
# The body served is still /index.html either way, so wouter's client-side
# router still renders the friendly NotFound page — only the HTTP status
# search engines and monitoring see is different.
/                   /index.html   200
/products           /index.html   200
/export-solutions   /index.html   200
/wholesale          /index.html   200
/export             /index.html   200
/about              /index.html   200
/contact            /index.html   200
/*                  /index.html   404
